{
  "schema": 1,
  "purpose": "PU-1 field classification of Alpaca broker/trading API responses. The broker API is a MIXED source: owner transaction/account records and marked-to-market market data arrive in the same response, so the host is not blanket NON_DATA. OWNER_RECORD fields map to owner_generated_records (COMMERCIAL_OK); MARKET_DATA fields map to alpaca_market_data (PERSONAL). Any field or response kind NOT listed here is classified MARKET_DATA (conservative). Used by app/licensing/broker_fields.py; the AST check in scripts/check_pu1_registry_closure.py enforces that modules reading the ast_enforced names go through that helper or are allowlisted with a reason.",
  "source_ids": {
    "OWNER_RECORD": "owner_generated_records",
    "MARKET_DATA": "alpaca_market_data"
  },
  "default_class": "MARKET_DATA",
  "ast_enforced_market_data_names": [
    "current_price",
    "market_value",
    "unrealized_pl",
    "unrealized_plpc",
    "unrealized_intraday_pl",
    "unrealized_intraday_plpc",
    "change_today",
    "lastday_price",
    "long_market_value",
    "short_market_value",
    "position_market_value",
    "portfolio_value",
    "last_equity",
    "buying_power",
    "regt_buying_power",
    "daytrading_buying_power",
    "non_marginable_buying_power"
  ],
  "ast_not_enforced_note": "'equity' and 'cash' are classified in the table but NOT AST-enforced: 'equity' is a pervasive non-broker key (backtest curves, snapshots) and enforcing it would be noise. Consumers of broker 'equity' must use the helper by convention and are covered by tests at the wired extraction points.",
